OL,3,GNEWSARare plaques discovered in hallway
OL,4,Aof family home
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo rare plaques have been sold for
OL,7,F#100,000 at auction in a "once in a
OL,8,Fgeneration" moment in art history.
OL,10,FFor years, a family in a small
OL,11,FShaftesbury home had enjoyed glancing
OL,12,Fup at the two pieces of art in their
OL,13,Fhallway - which depicted a scene of
OL,14,FCyrus the Great, founder of the
OL,15,FAchaemenid Empire.
OL,17,FIt was only when they emailed a picture
OL,18,Fto Wiltshire-based auctioneers Woolley
OL,19,Fand Wallis that they realised the
OL,20,Fplaques had been created by famed
OL,21,FRenaissance artist Francesco Xanto
OL,22,FAvelli who lived between 1487 and 1542.
OL,23,APub: 23-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,350,340,200,160,0,100
